  <static seed="110" source="Library/Michigan/Chap3Sec4/Q71.pg">
    <statement><p>Given
<m>F(1)=3, F'(1)=2, F(4)=5, F'(4)=5</m> and
<m>G(1)=4, G'(1)=4, G(3)=2, G'(3)=2</m>,
find each of the following.
(Enter <alert>dne</alert> for any derivative that cannot be
computed from this information alone.)</p>
<p><ol label="A.">
<li>
<p><m>H(1)</m>  if <m>H(x)=F(G(x))</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>H'(1)</m> if <m>H(x)=F(G(x))</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>H(1)</m>  if <m>H(x)=G(F(x))</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>H'(1)</m> if <m>H(x)=G(F(x))</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>H'(1)</m> if <m>H(x)=F(x)/G(x)</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5\cdot 4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\cdot 2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{2\cdot 4-3\cdot 4}{4^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>H(x) = F(G(x))</m>,



<m>H(1) = F(G(1)) = F(4) = 5</m>



<m>H'(1) = F'(G(1))\cdot G'(1) = F'(4)\cdot 4 = 
   5\cdot 4 = 20</m>



For <m>H(x) = G(F(x))</m>, 



<m>H(1) = G(F(1)) = G(3) = 2</m>



<m>H'(1) = G'(F(1))\cdot F'(1) = G'(3)\cdot 2 = 
   2\cdot 2 = 4</m>



For <m>H(x) = F(x)/G(x)</m>, 



<m>H'(1) = \frac{F'(1) G(1) - F(1) G'(1)}{G(1)^2}
   = \frac{ (2)(4) - (3)(4) } {4^2} = -0.25</m>.



</solution>
